"58f7e29b203c2cd62a842cc25bcff615999703d7be607fb923b66c1f4871848e","event_uuid":"f94852c3-472c-4b83-a2d5-4cff6902cffb","position":{"commit_sha":"3c10a60db4e3d2a400bee4eba94b66de9c36a773","position":"1788813532615195740-f94852c3-472c-4b83-a2d5-4cff6902cffb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"16b15d0f034a89a9a4495a769de0fff15cce9e6eaee6e29799aea894624427c2","event_uuid":"86a71941-4ff2-4b79-b0c1-3e0aa524e0bd","position":{"commit_sha":"098a7200d92e9ca5cbecf1ed004be2b5e532f10d","position":"1788815201059588183-86a71941-4ff2-4b79-b0c1-3e0aa524e0bd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bcebec773f35c40626870272fb174e72abafbd491327fefa4369eac272dea6eb","event_uuid":"ca6940b2-64b8-4d86-a7d1-513c870c3296","position":{"commit_sha":"3b7e408532431e618009a621f5eb1f2a62a6e39a","position":"1788816057464092473-ca6940b2-64b8-4d86-a7d1-513c870c3296"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"eec186d4af79fdf52a4e1ce1a16f69e085516af0240c4ef73a45f33c1540ae45","event_uuid":"baf75810-0889-4296-9fbd-0080520818b1","position":{"commit_sha":"ad75a0448e4d60371769a779e3ef5ed07da965f8","position":"1788819072578406144-baf75810-0889-4296-9fbd-0080520818b1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Design decision (standing authorization): choose a new closed discovery output model for the default `ready_tickets` response, while preserving `full=True` as the existing full `TicketStateOut` shape. Rationale: active OSS APIs commonly use lightweight list/discovery representations and reserve full resource representations for detail/explicit-expanded calls (for example GitHub list vs get responses and Kubernetes list item summaries with opt-in detail). This is the documented best-practice default here because it creates durable headroom instead of another narrow trim inside `TicketStateOut`, and it makes the default tool contract match the question the caller asks: \"what can I work on next?\"","timestamp":1788806249212705020},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: the first review BLOCKed on an incomplete affected-file inventory for the new `ready_tickets` outputSchema. I expanded file impact/scope to include the canonical schema file, output-schema docs, and the schema/read-surface contract tests that currently bind `ready_tickets` to `TicketStateOut`. Prior-art/default remains the lightweight-list + explicit-full-detail pattern: keep default discovery rows compact, preserve `full=True` for full ticket state.","timestamp":1788807523529318934}],"created_at":1787953792470677001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f3594632-ce17-43ec-8b50-3c9a071ce1cf","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0"},{"link_uuid":"f94852c3-472c-4b83-a2d5-4cff6902cffb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ed37-564b-67af-421d"},{"link_uuid":"86a71941-4ff2-4b79-b0c1-3e0aa524e0bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cbbc-6163-421b-4176"},{"link_uuid":"ca6940b2-64b8-4d86-a7d1-513c870c3296","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2059-1078-2d40-4a3a"},{"link_uuid":"baf75810-0889-4296-9fbd-0080520818b1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"776f-250f-e2a6-45d9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`ready_tickets` is bounded at 90,000 bytes by bug `daughterly-agitative-ocelot`\n(`494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0`), but even after that fix's lean projection it sits at **58 rows /\n87,893 wire bytes — roughly ONE row of headroom**. The bound is correct and its refusal is\nactionable (it points at `next_batch`), but the tool will begin refusing its default call\nabout as soon as one more ticket becomes ready. That is a cliff, not a fixed problem.\n\n`ready_tickets` is a discovery surface: it answers \"what can I work on next?\" A discovery\ncaller needs id, alias, title, type, status, priority, and blocking summary, not dependency\narrays, file-impact arrays, authorship, comments, or full ticket defaults. Measured on the real\nstore (58 ready rows, 90,000-byte budget):\n\n| shape | bytes/row | rows that fit | headroom vs today |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| as shipped (lean, `TicketStateOut`) | 1,515 | 59 | +1 |\n| lean minus `file_impact`/`deps`/author/env fields | 801 | 112 | +54 |\n| summary fields, still via `TicketStateOut` | 572 | 157 | +99 |\n| summary fields via a NEW closed output model | 234 | 384 | +326 |\n\nTwo findings drive this:\n\n1. **The lean ready row still carries fields a discovery caller cannot use.** `file_impact` is\n   252 B/row (18.1% of the row) and `deps` 160 B/row (11.5%) — 30% of the payload between them,\n   for a question that only needs discovery fields and blocking state.\n2. **`TicketStateOut`'s declared defaults set a floor.** Projecting to summary fields but\n   returning `TicketStateOut` still costs 572 B/row, because `model_validate` re-adds\n   `description: null`, `comments: []`, `deps: []`, `inbound_deps: []`, `file_impact: []`,\n   `file_impact_scope`, `no_file_impact_reason`, `plan_review_health: null` and\n   `cross_session_warning: null`. **338 of those 572 bytes are re-added defaults** — the same\n   mechanism that made the parent bug's budget under-estimate by 178%.\n\n## Approach\n\nImplement the durable fix: change the default `ready_tickets(full=False)` MCP response to a new\nclosed discovery output model with exactly the fields needed for choosing work (ticket id, alias,\ntitle, type, status, priority, and blocking summary). Keep `ready_tickets(full=True)` returning the\nexisting full `TicketStateOut` shape for callers that explicitly opt in to full details. This\nmirrors common actively maintained OSS API practice: list/discovery endpoints return compact item\nsummaries, while detail or explicit-expanded calls return the complete resource.\n\nDo not change `list_tickets` in this ticket. Its filters make an over-budget refusal actionable,\nso the budget is a guardrail there; `ready_tickets` has no narrowing arguments and needs a safer\ndefault shape. Document the output narrowing as its own release note and changelog entry because a\nnew output schema is a declared contract change rather than just another field omission under the\n`494b` axis.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` — select the discovery model for default `ready_tickets` and retain\n  the full model when `full=True`.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` — define the closed discovery output model/schema.\n- `src/rebar/schemas/ready_ticket_summary.schema.json` — add the canonical schema file for the\n  new public output model.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` — adjust only if the shared read projection needs a\n  matching discovery field set.\n- `docs/output-schemas.md` — update generated/schema documentation if the new public model changes\n  the output-schema inventory.\n- `docs/release-notes.md` — record the output contract narrowing and the `full=True` escape hatch.\n- `CHANGELOG.md` — add the user-facing changelog note.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py` — add the per-row-size regression.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py` — update the `ready_tickets`\n  canonical default schema and add/retain coverage that `full=True` validates as `TicketStateOut`.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py` — replace default-shape parity with the\n  deliberate asymmetry: `list_tickets` remains filterable/full enough by default, while\n  `ready_tickets` defaults to discovery and `ready_tickets(full=True)` remains full.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py` — keep model/schema drift\n  coverage current for the new public output model if the inventory requires an explicit example.\n- `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_outputs.py` — keep typed read-tool output schema coverage\n  aligned with the ready-tickets default schema change.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED first: add a regression in `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py` that\n  fails on current `main` because default `ready_tickets` rows exceed the discovery per-row ceiling\n  after `model_validate` and `js_safe_result`.\n- Happy path: default `ready_tickets` returns discovery-shaped rows and the measured wire payload has\n  at least 3x current-store headroom.\n- Compatibility path: `ready_tickets(full=True)` still returns full `TicketStateOut` rows with fields\n  such as `deps`/`file_impact` available.\n- Schema wiring: `test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py`, `test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py`,\n  and `test_schema_outputs.py` pass with the new canonical discovery schema.\n- Documentation: release notes and changelog name the contract change and the `full=True` escape\n  hatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A decision is recorded on the ticket to use a new closed discovery output model for default\n      `ready_tickets`, with `full=True` continuing to return full `TicketStateOut` rows.\n- [ ] Default `ready_tickets` has headroom for at least 3x the current ready count on this store,\n      measured on the wire payload after `model_validate` and `js_safe_result`; verified by a\n      regression test in `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py`.\n- [ ] The new public discovery output model has a canonical schema file and the MCP schema coverage\n      tests validate default `ready_tickets` against that schema.\n- [ ] `ready_tickets(full=True)` remains compatible with the previous full `TicketStateOut` shape and\n      is covered by a contract/read-surface test.\n- [ ] The output-schema change is recorded in `docs/release-notes.md`.\n- [ ] The output-schema change is recorded in `CHANGELOG.md`.\n- [ ] `list_tickets` is explicitly left unchanged because its filter arguments make over-budget\n      refusal actionable; this asymmetry is documented in the change.\n- [ ] Regression coverage asserts the per-row size ceiling so default ready rows cannot silently\n      re-grow.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"Select the discovery output model for default ready_tickets and retain full model when full=True."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"Define the closed discovery output model used by default ready_tickets."},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/ready_ticket_summary.schema.json","reason":"Canonical schema file for the new public discovery output model."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py","reason":"Adjust only if the shared read projection needs a matching discovery field set."},{"path":"docs/output-schemas.md","reason":"Document the new ready_tickets discovery output schema, if generated schema docs require it."},{"path":"docs/release-notes.md","reason":"Record the output contract narrowing and full=True compatibility path."},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","reason":"User-facing changelog entry for the ready_tickets default shape change."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_payload_budget.py","reason":"Per-row wire-size regression coverage for default ready_tickets."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","reason":"Update the ready_tickets canonical default schema and validate full=True against TicketStateOut."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py","reason":"Replace default-shape parity with deliberate ready_tickets discovery/default versus list/full asymmetry coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_model_schema_drift_heldout.py","reason":"Keep model/schema drift coverage current for the new public output model if its enumerations require explicit examples."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_schema_outputs.py","reason":"Keep typed read-tool output schema coverage aligned with the ready_tickets default schema change."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2059-1078-2d40-4a3a"],["relates_to","776f-250f-e2a6-45d9"],["relates_to","cbbc-6163-421b-4176"],["relates_to","ed37-564b-67af-421d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"20536924-0a68-4b5d-83a4-fd6d5378dbca","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"0c99-8f2b-0de7-48f2","ticket_type":"story","title":"Give ready_tickets a discovery-shaped result so its budget stops being a cliff","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["06ecdb41-57c3-4d71-aa4f-ff21731c98bf","32745768-9c91-4c74-bafb-5886825d1bf8","dc4c46d5-138d-4910-9fe5-7dd64ea582e4","6090a00b-eae9-45f4-bd29-a7005be24103","5cb43854-4957-4853-bcc7-fbe78